     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Friday, June 8, 2018 at 7:46:05 PM UTC+3, Zhian Kamvar wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Meki,</div><div><br></div><div>Your data are coded in the correct format for the genlight objects. You should read adegenet&#39;s &quot;genomics&quot; tutorial: <a href=\"https://github.com/thibautjombart/adegenet/wiki/Tutorials\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/thibautjombart/adegenet/wiki/Tutorials&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480533701000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3rq7VCHrm4GLYX4Xy583KE\">https://github.com/thibautjombart/adegenet/wiki/Tutorials</a>. Moreover, because AMOVA requires population strata, you should read the &quot;strata&quot; tutorial in the page I just linked.</div><div><br></div><div>Before you start AMOVA, you should also read the AMOVA manual page for poppr: <a href=\"https://grunwaldlab.github.io/poppr/reference/poppr.amova.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://grunwaldlab.github.io/poppr/reference/poppr.amova.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480533701000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2QMCxxviOlk-3F8zvIalpF\">https://grunwaldlab.github.io/poppr/reference/poppr.amova.html</a></div><div><br></div><div>To prepare your data specifically, you will need to do three steps:</div><div><br></div><div>1. read the data in with read.table</div><div>2. extract the genotype matrix without the metadata and transpose it</div><div>3. convert these data to a genlight object<br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;poppr&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Data path can be a path on your computer</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>data_path </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/poppr/attach/3753c7045bd07/example%20data.csv?part=0.1&amp;authuser=0\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/poppr/attach/3753c7045bd07/example%2520data.csv?part%3D0.1%26authuser%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480533701000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1C4rd70hn7XKvbQoBvrOxA\">https://groups.google.com/group/poppr/attach/3753c7045bd07/example%20data.csv?part=0.1&amp;authuser=0</a>&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Extract first line containing pouplations, split it by comma, and then remove the first empty string</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>my_populations </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> strsplit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">readLines</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data_path</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1L</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;,&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)[[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]][-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Read the data into a data frame</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>myData </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">table</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data_path</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sep </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;,&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> skip </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1L</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> header </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Create a new genlight by transposing the data, assigning the locus names and strata</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>myData</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gl </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">new</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;genlight&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">myData</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                 loc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">names </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> myData$ID</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                 strata </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">population </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> my_populations</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># AMOVA</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>poppr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">amova</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">myData</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">population</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Hope that helps,</div><div>Zhian<br></div><div><br></div>On Wednesday, June 6, 2018 at 7:06:02 AM UTC-7, Meki Shehabu wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px\"><span style=\"margin:0px;font-family:NimbusRomNo9L-Regu;font-size:10pt\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></p><p style=\"margin:0px\"><span style=\"margin:0px;font-family:NimbusRomNo9L-Regu;font-size:10pt\"><font color=\"#000000\">I have SNP data, codded as 0\r\n(absence of SNP allele), 1 (one SNP allele, heterozygous form), 2 (presence of\r\n2 SNP alleles)</font></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px\"><span style=\"margin:0px;font-family:NimbusRomNo9L-Regu;font-size:10pt\"><font color=\"#000000\">I run structure analysis and\r\nidentified the populations</font></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px\"><span style=\"margin:0px;font-family:NimbusRomNo9L-Regu;font-size:10pt\"><font color=\"#000000\">I have attached an example data,\r\nwith 30 markers and 10 samples(genotypes). It has 3 populations, missing data\r\nis coded as NA</font></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px\"><span style=\"margin:0px;font-family:NimbusRomNo9L-Regu;font-size:10pt\"><font color=\"#000000\"> </font></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px\"><span style=\